OL,3,AAfrica's richest man launches
OL,4,Acontinent's biggest share sale
OL,5,
OL,6,FNigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote has
OL,7,Flaunched Africa's largest ever share
OL,8,Fsale, offering a stake in his oil
OL,9,Frefinery to the general public in a
OL,10,Fdeal that could raise as much as $2.1bn
OL,11,F(#1.6bn).
OL,13,FThe initial public offering (IPO) is
OL,14,Ffor roughly 3% of the Dangote refinery,
OL,15,Fwith the billionaire saying he wanted
OL,16,Fto give ordinary Nigerians the chance
OL,17,Fto share in the plant's success.
OL,19,FThe refinery, which started production
OL,20,Fin 2024, is one of the largest in the
OL,21,Fworld and took more than a decade to
OL,22,Fcomplete.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
